  "prefLabel": "Fis 1109.07 Legal Address",
  "recordType": "rule-section",
  "ruleText": "Fis 1109.07 Legal Address. Whenever an applicant is required to furnish his or her address by statute or rule, the address shall reflect a street, road, avenue, or like designation. A post office or rural route box number, without more, shall not be adequate.\n\nSource. #12785, eff 5-22-19",
  "source": "https://github.com/GraniteState/adm-rules-data/blob/1c92d82e0f03a582ca5b7a578588edf38de2318e/raw/2026-11-15/state_agencies/fis1100.html"
